- indexmap 2.14.0, Apache-2.0 OR MIT (`vendor/indexmap/`)
- winit 0.30.13, Apache-2.0 (`crates/aterm-window/`)

Each of these crates retains its upstream license text. The winit copy is
absorbed: it is `crates/aterm-window/` (its cargo package is still named
`winit`), a workspace member aterm owns and changes like its own code. It
contains aterm modifications to macOS application behavior, Wayland
seat/data-device handling, and Windows modal size/move event delivery (a
WM_TIMER pump so timed events keep flowing during caption drags and edge
resizes); its macOS backend runs on aterm's own Objective-C layer, its Windows
backend is ported to windows-sys 0.61, its Android, iOS, Orbital and Web
backends are removed, its Wayland KDE blur support is an opt-in feature, and it
defines its own key-text `SmolStr`. Its `dpi` module is derived from dpi 0.1.2
(Apache-2.0, from the winit project; only the crate's Apache-2.0 part), and its
`CursorIcon` from cursor-icon 1.2.0 by Kirill Chibisov (MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR
Zlib, used under Apache-2.0). Modified and added files carry prominent notices.

`crates/aterm-lz4/` is a modified, block-mode-only subset derived from
lz4_flex 0.11.5 by Pascal Seitz and contributors. Its upstream-derived files
are MIT-licensed and carry local compatibility, lint, and verification changes.
See `crates/aterm-lz4/LICENSE-MIT`.

`crates/aterm-zstd/src/decode/` carries a modified, decode-only subset of
ruzstd 0.8.3 by Moritz Borcherding and contributors (no encoder, no
dictionaries, a bounds-checked window in place of its unsafe ring buffer).
Its upstream-derived files are MIT-licensed and say which upstream file each
derives from. See `crates/aterm-zstd/LICENSE-MIT`.

`crates/aterm-serde/` is a modified, std-only subset derived from serde_core
1.0.228 and serde 1.0.228 by Erick Tryzelaar, David Tolnay and contributors,
licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0. Its test suite is ported from serde's
`test_suite` (v1.0.228) on a harness derived from serde_test 1.0.177, under the
same terms. Each derived file names its upstream file. See
`crates/aterm-serde/LICENSE-MIT` and `crates/aterm-serde/LICENSE-APACHE`.

`crates/aterm-serde-derive/` generates the code serde_derive 1.0.228 by Erick
Tryzelaar, David Tolnay and contributors generates, licensed MIT OR
Apache-2.0: its attribute handling and code generation are derived from
serde_derive's, for the subset of attributes aterm uses, and each derived file
names its upstream file. The parser underneath it,
`crates/aterm-macro-support/`, is aterm's own. See
`crates/aterm-serde-derive/LICENSE-MIT` and
`crates/aterm-serde-derive/LICENSE-APACHE`.

`crates/aterm-wasm-abi/src/panic_hook.rs` is derived from
console_error_panic_hook 0.1.7 by Nick Fitzgerald, licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0,
and names the file it came from. See `crates/aterm-wasm-abi/LICENSE-MIT` and
`crates/aterm-wasm-abi/LICENSE-APACHE`.

`crates/aterm-win32/` is generated from windows-sys 0.61.2 by Microsoft
Corporation (the windows-rs project), licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0: `src/core.rs`,
`src/Win32.rs` and `src/Win32/` hold the subset of upstream's declarations
aterm's Windows graph reads, and its `link!` macro is derived from windows-link
0.2.1 (the same project, under the same terms). Each generated file names the
upstream file it came from. See `crates/aterm-win32/LICENSE-MIT` and
`crates/aterm-win32/LICENSE-APACHE`.

`crates/aterm-font/` is a modified subset derived from ttf-parser 0.25.1 by
Yevhenii Reizner and contributors, licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0: its sfnt,
cmap, metrics (head/hhea/maxp/hmtx/vhea/VORG/post), glyf/loca/gvar,
CFF/CFF2, variation-table (fvar/avar/HVAR/VVAR/MVAR and the item variation
store), OS/2, name, kern, COLR/CPAL, sbix, CBLC/CBDT (with EBLC/EBDT and
bloc/bdat) and OpenType layout (GSUB/GDEF) readers, and the `Face` methods
over them, with aterm's never-panic hardening. Each derived file names its
upstream file. See `crates/aterm-font/LICENSE-MIT` and
`crates/aterm-font/LICENSE-APACHE`.

`crates/aterm-font/src/shape/` is a modified subset derived from rustybuzz
0.20.1 (Copyright HarfBuzz developers and 2020 Yevhenii Reizner, a port of
HarfBuzz), licensed MIT: its buffer, feature map and shape plan, GSUB
application (lookup types 1 to 8, the skipping iterator, (chained) context
lookups and ligature formation), set digest, OpenType script tags and the
Arabic shaper with its joining table, cut to what a terminal reaches. Each
derived file names its upstream file. See `crates/aterm-font/LICENSE-RUSTYBUZZ`.

`crates/aterm-font/src/autohint/` is a modified subset derived from skrifa
0.46.2, read-fonts 0.43.2 and font-types 0.12.4 (Copyright 2019 Fontations
Developers; skrifa's autohinter is a port of FreeType's autofit), licensed MIT
OR Apache-2.0, used here under MIT: the automatic hinter (glyph styles and
their `GSUB` coverage, stem widths and blue zones, segments, edges and their
grid fitting, point interpolation, FreeType's path decomposition) and the
FreeType-style unscaled `glyf`/`gvar` loader, `cmap` subtable selection and
fixed-point normalization it reads outlines through, without the TrueType
interpreter, the CFF hinter or the hint-plan recorder. Each derived file
names its upstream file. See `crates/aterm-font/LICENSE-FONTATIONS`.

`crates/aterm-verify/src/wasm_glue/templates.rs` and
`crates/aterm-verify/src/wasm_glue/js.rs` carry JS derived from the glue
wasm-bindgen-cli-support 0.2.108 writes (src/js/mod.rs and src/js/binding.rs;
Alex Crichton and the wasm-bindgen contributors, licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0):
the string and array helpers, the cached memory views, the class shape, the
`--target web` loader, the import shims and the shape of each export's
binding. The glue `verify glue` writes carries them too. See
`crates/aterm-verify/LICENSE-MIT`.

